ion with expert assistance and recurring briefings from the Emergency Relief Coordinator.\n\nIndia objected, warning of diversion risks and seeking proactive involvement by the 1267 Monitoring Team and robust reporting mechanisms. India judged these concerns not fully addressed in the adopted text, urging stronger oversight within the existing framework. The Council's safeguards, including due diligence requirements and the 1267 Committee's monitoring role, were intended to ensure oversight while allowing time for targeted measures. The Council's actions established the exemption and monitoring framework; India's assessment remained that the adopted text lacked sufficient proactive oversight mechanisms to fully address diversion risks.", "input_tokens": 386, "output_tokens": 220, "termination": "cap"}}
